# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: PCSX ReARMed.
Package: PCSX
Section: Emulation
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Components: Apps.Emulation.!PCSX (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-pcsx
Description: PlayStation emulator (PCSX ReARMed)
 PCSX ReARMed with a native desktop frontend: full speed on a Pi 4
 with its ARM recompiler and NEON renderer, a scalable window or full
 screen, sound, keyboard and USB game pads, save states, memory cards
 and a games library. Plays .cue/.bin, .chd, .pbp, .iso, CloneCD and
 games inside .zip and .7z files. A built-in BIOS replacement runs most
 games. Needs ARMv7 with NEON. Use only discs and BIOS images you own.
 PlayStation is a trademark of Sony Interactive Entertainment; this
 port isn't connected with Sony.
